# Inert until collections-as-call-arguments lands (sub-bindings are numeric-only) — see Future.md. The fold itself is proven equivalent to the C++ reducer (tests.cpp).
# product_of(xs) — product of a seq collection, as a foldl over the mul operator.
# SPEC definition; coexists with the C++ `product` fast-path and is proven
# equivalent. Empty collection -> 1 (the mul identity / fold seed).
@include "mul.fw"
[product_of(xs) -> result]
result = foldl(xs, mul, 1)
